WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.310
SPEAKER: Access control
capability in Security Command

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.920
Center allows organization
administrators

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.650
to grant fine-grained
access to the assets

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:17.310
and findings surfaced in
Security Command Center.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.320
This feature is relevant
for many use cases,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.220
including sensitive
applications or compliance

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:26.160
regimes that require
strict access controls,

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.410
as it lets you isolate
Cloud resources

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.260
and restrict employee
access to only those they

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.910
need to do their jobs.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.460
Access control at the
folder and project level

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.240
is available to Security Command
Center Premium customers.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.220
In this video, we'll
walk through how

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.370
to grant granular access
control to assets and findings

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.830
in your organization,
and demonstrate

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.130
the experience from the
end user's perspective.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:53.370
Starting in the Organization
view of the Security Command

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:56.520
Center, you can see this
example organization

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:58.500
has thousands of assets.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.350
And similarly, it
has many findings,

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:04.379
rather than providing
organization-wide permissions.

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:06.540
Administrators can
use access control

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.630
to limit the View or Edit
permissions in Security Command

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.660
Center to specific
folders and projects.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.550
We'll now show
how to grant users

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.770
access to specific
folders or projects

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:19.980
in Security Command Center
using the Cloud Console.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.000
In the Project
Selector dropdown,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.180
choose the project or
folder to which you would

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.950
like to provide scoped access.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.800
In this case, we're
selecting a project.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.510
Then, head to the
IAM landing page,

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:35.060
which you can find with the
left-hand navigation menu.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:40.680
Search for the user's email
address, and click to edit.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:44.580
Then add the Security
Center Admin Editor, Viewer,

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.520
or one of the many additional
Security Center roles

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.110
based on your user's needs.

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:50.820
Then click Save.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.210
The permissions are now
applied and live for your user.

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.780
Now, let's switch over to
view the console logged

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.400
in as the user.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.410
As you can see,
when the user tries

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.320
to access Security Command
Center for the organization

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:07.930
itself, they will get a
Permission Denied error

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.419
because they do not have
permissions at the organization

00:02:10.419 --> 00:02:11.290
level.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.150
Using the Project
dropdown, we'll

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.790
select the target project
to which they were granted

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:18.040
Security Command Center access.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.900
We'll now see Security
Command Center

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:21.950
is scoped to the
specific project,

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:24.940
including only the assets and
findings that are associated

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.290
with the project.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:29.000
For example, by
selecting the Assets tab,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.790
we can now see that
the number of assets

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:32.620
has decreased from
the Organization

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:36.580
view we saw earlier, as now,
these are only the assets that

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.890
reside within this project.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:41.140
When looking at
projects, we can only

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:45.190
see the specific project and not
others within the organization.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:48.160
We'll click on a specific
asset, such as this bucket,

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.250
to expand the asset details.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.230
Take note of the
new Canonical Name

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.350
field, which contains the
asset's actual parent project

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.010
ID and its name.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.340
Now, let's head to
the Findings tab.

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.410
Again, we can only
see findings that

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.530
are associated with the assets
contained in this project,

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:09.260
rather than the
organization-wide findings.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.050
Note-- if we had shared
access at the folder level,

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:14.810
we would be able to see
assets and findings associated

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:18.120
with all projects
within that folder.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.860
Just as we saw earlier
in the Assets tab,

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.740
we can see that the
details for a finding

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.140
includes the new Canonical
Name field, which

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.650
identifies the parent project
associated with the finding.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:30.840
All functionality
across dashboards

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.600
is scoped as per the
access controls defined.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.640
For example, in
the Overview tab,

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:38.490
we continue to see the charts
and reports for findings

00:03:38.490 --> 00:03:40.560
within the scope
of this project.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.110
And we also see only
the vulnerabilities

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.300
associated with this project.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.870
The Settings page, however,
does require organization level

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.360
permissions in order to
be viewed and edited.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.700
Because Security Command
Center settings always

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.220
apply to the entire
organization.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.570
Congratulations.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.510
You're now equipped to use
Access Control in Security

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.430
Command Center to
restrict users,

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:06.240
to manage assets and findings
within an assigned scope.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.290
[MUSIC PLAYING]

